1
00:00:28,533 --> 00:00:35,244
Heavy nights, grey days. Shadow walks behind the glass.

2
00:00:35,377 --> 00:00:42,399
Broken heart, no more blood. Passenger with a faded card.

3
00:00:44,888 --> 00:00:51,333
Doorbell rings, sharp and clear. Silver chime hits me here.

4
00:00:51,822 --> 00:01:00,044
Lands inside my quiet chest. Something starts… I feel the rest.

5
00:01:02,066 --> 00:01:08,333
Francien opens, apron tight. Wind and morning in the light.

6
00:01:08,476 --> 00:01:16,609
Pastor stands on old black bike. Red cold cheeks, warm smile bright.

7
00:01:18,466 --> 00:01:24,911
“Heard you play Bach all alone. Lonely boy reaching for home.

8
00:01:25,133 --> 00:01:33,577
Children’s choir needs your hands. Come and take your place and stand.”

9
00:01:33,827 --> 00:01:40,360
Let the silver chime ring deep. Wake the music I must keep.

10
00:01:40,538 --> 00:01:46,671
Tame the organ, wood and keys. Play it faster, set me free.

11
00:01:47,071 --> 00:01:53,516
Rise above the dark tonight. Let the children sing so bright.

12
00:01:53,738 --> 00:01:59,427
But the echo soft and true…

13
00:01:59,693 --> 00:02:08,538
Did I ever choose for you?

14
00:02:38,705 --> 00:02:44,616
Moped coughs through streets of ice. Wind cuts sharp like frozen knives.

15
00:02:45,149 --> 00:02:53,016
Coffee smell, the heavy door. Thirty eyes stare at the floor.

16
00:02:55,193 --> 00:03:01,593
“Bach boy… is it really you?” I sit down, my fingers fly true.

17
00:03:01,905 --> 00:03:08,260
Room goes quiet, holds its breath in the pale cold winter death.

18
00:03:08,749 --> 00:03:14,393
Holy night, the stars above. Church is full of light and love.

19
00:03:14,993 --> 00:03:21,571
Candles glow and incense rises. Golden lights on all our faces.

20
00:03:21,705 --> 00:03:28,060
Vermeulen waits, strong and old. Wooden beast with pipes of gold.

21
00:03:28,416 --> 00:03:36,593
Silver voices ready, strong. Time to play the sacred song.

22
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:43,257
Let the silver chime ring deep.
Wake the music I must keep.

23
00:03:43,947 --> 00:03:50,036
Tame the organ, wood and keys. Play it faster, set me free.

24
00:03:50,525 --> 00:03:56,925
Rise above the dark tonight.
Let the children sing so bright.

25
00:03:57,236 --> 00:04:02,569
But the echo soft and true…

26
00:04:02,953 --> 00:04:08,642
Did I ever choose for you?

27
00:04:08,848 --> 00:04:14,848
One high note floats all alone. “Holy Night” calls angels home.

28
00:04:15,115 --> 00:04:23,070
Four years old, her hand in mine. Little crib in candle shine.

29
00:04:25,026 --> 00:04:31,470
“Paul, you see Him small but whole?” I look down into her soul.

30
00:04:31,604 --> 00:04:48,359
Same sweet tears she cried before fall again… forevermore.

31
00:04:48,462 --> 00:04:54,817
Last chord dies, the walls shake loud. Applause comes crashing like a crowd.

32
00:04:55,173 --> 00:05:01,350
Pastor’s hand upon my frame. “You made heaven sing His name.”

33
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:07,138
My family smile. They call it miracle, worthwhile.

34
00:05:07,462 --> 00:05:17,062
But deep inside I feel it start… the ending opening my heart.

35
00:05:18,593 --> 00:05:24,326
A noble start for them… For me the end began.

36
00:05:25,451 --> 00:05:31,895
Let the silver chime ring deep. Wake the music I must keep.

37
00:05:31,905 --> 00:05:38,439
Tame the organ, wood and keys. Play it faster, set me free.

38
00:05:38,562 --> 00:05:45,362
Rise above the dark tonight.
Let the children sing so bright.

39
00:05:45,372 --> 00:05:51,505
But the echo soft and true…

40
00:05:54,542 --> 00:06:06,008
Did I ever choose for you?

